.TH "ODIR-GUI" "7" "" "odir 25.1.2+onesimus.0.2.0" "Onesimus Director Commands"
.SH NAME
odir\-gui \- gui: Switch between interactive (gui off) and non\-interactive (gui on) mode
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
gui [<on|off>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
gui on switches the session into a mode for graphical front ends and scripts, gui off back to the interactive default. In GUI mode the Director silently uses the first catalog of the configuration when no catalog= is given, prints catalog numbers without thousands separators and left aligned, and omits the "You have messages." hint.
.PP
The setting applies only to the own session until it ends. Case does not matter; the first word that reads on or off counts.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.SS "gui"
.TP
.B "<on|off>"
Switch on or off (positional value; values: on, off)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B "gui on"
machine friendly output without catalog prompts
.TP
.B "gui off"
back to interactive mode
.SH ORIGIN
Bareos console command.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR odir\-commands (7),
.BR oconsole (1)
